[statement]
A stream whose first block has neither magic nor a checksum that matches is
not a tar archive: here, the signature of a PNG image followed by zeros.
ferrotape reports that the stream is not a tar archive, which a caller can
tell apart from a damaged one.

[archive]
bytes "\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n"
bytes "\0"*1016

[verdict]
all: refused NotATar at 0

[gnu-tar 1.35]
warning "tar: This does not look like a tar archive"
warning "tar: Skipping to next header"
warning "tar: A lone zero block at 2"
warning "tar: Exiting with failure status due to previous errors"
exit 2

[bsdtar 3.8.11]
warning "bsdtar: Error opening archive: Unrecognized archive format"
exit 1

[python 3.12.3]
error "ReadError: bad checksum"

[go 1.27.0]
error "archive/tar: invalid tar header"
